{"book":8,"chapter":3,"context":{"chapter":3,"title":"At the Threshing Floor","summary":"Naomi sends Ruth to the threshing floor at night to ask Boaz to marry her. Boaz praises her loyalty and agrees to act, but explains that a nearer relative has the first right. He sends her home at dawn with a generous gift of barley.","background":"A threshing floor was a stretch of hard, open ground where grain was beaten, then tossed into the evening breeze so the wind carried off the chaff (v. 2); owners often slept there to guard the harvest. Ruth's words, 'spread therefore thy skirt over thine handmaid' (v. 9), asked for marriage and protection (compare Ezekiel 16:8).","customs":[{"term":"Spread thy skirt","verses":"3:9","note":"'Skirt' here is the corner of a garment, the same Hebrew word as 'wings' in 2:12. Ruth asks Boaz to be the answer to his own prayer."}],"watchFor":["Boaz calls her 'a virtuous woman' (v. 11), the same phrase used in Proverbs 31:10.","He praises her 'kindness' (v. 10), Hebrew hesed, loyal love.","'Go not empty unto thy mother in law' (v. 17), answering Naomi's 'empty' in 1:21."],"connections":["Ruth 2:12","Deuteronomy 25:5-6","Ezekiel 16:8","Proverbs 31:10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַתֹּאמֶר","vatomer","H559","Hc/Vqw3fs","and she said"],["לָהּ","lah","H9034","HRd/Sp3fs","to <the> her"],["נָעֳמִי","no'omi","H5281","HNpf","Naomi"],["חֲמוֹתָהּ","chamotah","H2545","HNcfsc/Sp3fs","mother-in-law her"],["בִּתִּי","biti","H1323","HNcfsc/Sp1bs","O daughter my"],["הֲלֹא","halo'","H3808","HTi/Tn","¿ not"],["אֲבַקֶּשׁ","'avakesh-","H1245","HVpi1cs","will I seek"],["לָךְ","lakh","H9032","HRd/Sp2fs","for <the> you"],["מָנוֹחַ","manoach","H4494","HNcmsa","a resting place"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","that"],["יִיטַב","yitav-","H3190","HVqi3ms","it will go well"],["לָךְ","lakh","H9032","HRd/Sp2fs","for <the> you"]],"x":[[8001009,8001009,28],[54005008,54005008,26],[19128002,19128002,20],[54005014,54005014,20],[46007036,46007036,14],[5004040,5004040,13],[24022015,